From: futurestandard local patches
Subject: [PATCH] mpegtsmux: write a packet without a timestamp as payload only

A buffer that carries neither PTS nor DTS can reach the muxer: h264parse
emits one after a broken NAL, which an interrupted RTSP link produces.
tsmux_write_stream_packet() then computed cur_ts as CLOCK_BASE plus
G_MININT64, a huge negative number. With a bitrate set, pad_stream() saw a
negative difference to the stream's first timestamp, gst_util_uint64_scale()
took it as a huge unsigned divisor, the bitrate came out as zero and the
padding loop never ended: it allocated null packets until the process was
killed for memory, 4 GB in about seven seconds at 9 Mbps. Without a bitrate
the same value reached the PCR.

A packet whose stream has no timestamp is now written as payload only, with
no PAT/PMT rewrite, no padding and no PCR; the next packet with a timestamp
carries on from the byte counter, so a constant bitrate catches up over the
gap. pad_stream() also refuses a timestamp that is not ahead of the first
one, which covers a timeline that steps back after a resync.

diff -ru a/_p2_/gst/mpegtsmux/tsmux/tsmux.c b/_p2_/gst/mpegtsmux/tsmux/tsmux.c
--- a/_p2_/gst/mpegtsmux/tsmux/tsmux.c	2026-09-28 17:37:29.965665448 +0900
+++ b/_p2_/gst/mpegtsmux/tsmux/tsmux.c	2026-09-28 17:37:29.977783377 +0900
@@ -1515,8 +1515,11 @@
   if (!GST_CLOCK_STIME_IS_VALID (stream->first_ts))
     stream->first_ts = cur_ts;
 
+  /* A timestamp that is not ahead of the first one has nothing to pad up
+   * to. Padding against it would compute a bitrate of zero, unsigned, and
+   * never stop. */
   diff = GST_CLOCK_DIFF (stream->first_ts, cur_ts);
-  if (diff == 0)
+  if (diff <= 0)
     goto done;
 
   ret = FALSE;
@@ -1621,12 +1624,17 @@
   g_return_val_if_fail (mux != NULL, FALSE);
   g_return_val_if_fail (stream != NULL, FALSE);
 
-  if (tsmux_stream_is_pcr (stream) || stream->program->pcr_pid) {
-    gint64 cur_ts = CLOCK_BASE;
-    if (tsmux_stream_get_dts (stream) != G_MININT64)
-      cur_ts += tsmux_stream_get_dts (stream);
-    else
-      cur_ts += tsmux_stream_get_pts (stream);
+  gint64 cur_ts = G_MININT64;
+  if (tsmux_stream_get_dts (stream) != G_MININT64)
+    cur_ts = CLOCK_BASE + tsmux_stream_get_dts (stream);
+  else if (tsmux_stream_get_pts (stream) != G_MININT64)
+    cur_ts = CLOCK_BASE + tsmux_stream_get_pts (stream);
+
+  /* Without a timestamp the packet is payload only: there is no time to
+   * pad up to, and a PCR derived from nothing would be wrong. The next
+   * timed packet carries on from the byte counter. */
+  if (cur_ts != G_MININT64 &&
+      (tsmux_stream_is_pcr (stream) || stream->program->pcr_pid)) {
 
     if (!rewrite_si (mux, cur_ts))
       goto fail;
